            <ArticleTitle>Fluoroscope-guided celiac plexus block in a pregnant patient: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jclinane.2014.06.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0952-8180(14)00317-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 28-weeks gestation pregnant patient with chronic pacreatitis and severe abdominal pain leading to impaired nutrition is presented. After detailed consideration of the case, fluoroscopic-guided celiac plexus neurolysis was performed. The block was performed using the transaortic approach as it reduces radiation exposure.</AbstractText>
